        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "43f45fd8-8f3d-5401-955c-bb30250ca97c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Symbols: Columns of Gediminas, Pillars of Gediminas\n- Places: Lithuania\n- Organizations: Lithuanian Republic\n- Products: Order of the Lithuanian Grand Duke Gediminas, Litas coins, military equipment\n- Events: World War I, World War II\n\nFacts:\n- The Columns of Gediminas, also called the Pillars of Gediminas, are one of the earliest symbols of Lithuania and one of its historical coats of arms.\n- During the period between World War I and World War II, the Lithuanian Republic used the Columns of Gediminas as a minor state symbol on items such as Litas coins and military equipment.\n- The Order of the Lithuanian Grand Duke Gediminas features the Columns of Gediminas, which are one of the national symbols of Lithuania.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
